{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791705726,"nonce":"wvG3EC62dL8+caXk6asUKy6tyq8=","title":"Toggles lag, and reactivity seems stuck, after many presses","message":"Reported by the user: \"toggle switch and checkbox examples show lag after multiple interactions\", and \"Reactivity might be getting stuck intermittently after multiple clicks.\"\n\nWhat explains \"stuck\": layout animations were not measured in a frame whose restyle started a transition (the `||=` in Layout.settleMotion, fixed in f1e89b6), so a switch's knob stayed where it was drawn until the next layout that started no transition, which a mouse move caused: the state had changed, the drawing had not.\n\nSince then the switch's knob moves by a transform, not a layout move (a956964).\n\nadapters/test/wiki-stress.mjs presses the toggles page's five controls in a seeded random order, with frames as a window makes them and sometimes before the last press's motion has played, and after each press checks every control and readout against a model; every 25 presses it lets motion settle and reads where the first knob is drawn. It also requires that a press does not slow (median of the last 50 within twice the median of presses 10 to 60, plus 2 ms) and that the heap holds steady (under 32 MB more, after GC).\n\nRuns: seeds 20261011, 1, 7, 99 at 300 presses and 4242 at 1000 all matched, with no slowdown (about 25 to 31 ms a press including its frames) and about 1 MB of heap growth. Mutation: without the rule that moves the checked knob, it fails at step 149 on where the knob is drawn. No lag or stuck state reproduces now; reopen with a seed if one does.","files":null}]}